  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the hetionet dataset suggests a potential relationship between Guanidine and Kcnc3, based on shared interactions with Voltage-Gated Potassium Channels. The scores for all three paths are identical, indicating a consistent level of confidence in the association. Guanidine is shown to bind to three different potassium channel proteins—Kcna7, Kcnv2, and Kcnh3—each of which is involved in the regulation of voltage-gated potassium channels. These channels are ultimately associated with Kcnc3, suggesting a possible pathway where Guanidine may influence Kcnc3 through its interaction with these intermediate proteins. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear, as the specific molecular mechanisms by which Guanidine affects Kcnc3 are not fully elucidated. The consistency across the three paths strengthens the hypothesis, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the biological relevance of this relationship.",
